---

# Working with Zones

## What a Zone Is
A **zone** is a scope that sits *above* realms. A realm is addressed as `cid.pid`; a zone is addressed as `cid.zid`. A zone-scoped service/storage/extension is deployed once per **zone** rather than per realm, and it authenticates as `cid.zid` instead of `cid.pid` (the zone id rides the PID slot as `ZONE_<zid>`, which the gateway detects).

Everything zone-related is selected by a single csproj property, `<BeamServiceScope>zone</BeamServiceScope>`, or the `--zone` flag on the `project new` commands / the `--scope zone` flag on `deploy`. When the property is absent the project is **realm**-scoped (the default).

## When to Use This Skill
- Creating a service, storage, or portal extension that should run per-zone (`cid.zid`) instead of per-realm.
- Deploying to a zone manifest (`deploy … --scope zone`).
- Inspecting which local projects are zone- vs realm-scoped (`project ps`).
- Writing a zone service that reaches into a realm (`AssumeRealm`) or its own zone storage.
- Building a zone portal extension and calling a zone service from it.

## Creating Zone-Scoped Projects

All three `project new` commands take `--zone`. This stamps `<BeamServiceScope>zone</BeamServiceScope>` into the generated csproj (a service additionally inherits `ZoneMicroservice` instead of `Microservice`).

```
beam_exec("project new service MyZoneService --zone -q")
beam_exec("project new storage MyZoneStorage --zone -q")
beam_exec("project new portal-extension MyZonePanel --zone -q")
```
