### Scope must be consistent across a dependency
A service can only depend on a storage in the **same scope** — a zone storage may only be linked to zone services, and a realm storage only to realm services (they deploy into different manifests). The CLI enforces this: `project new`'s dependency prompt only offers same-scope candidates, and `project deps add` rejects a cross-scope link.

```
beam_exec("project deps add MyZoneService MyZoneStorage -q")
```

## Running & Inspecting Locally

`project ps` reports a **scope** column for every service, storage, and portal extension, so you can see zone vs realm at a glance.

```
beam_exec("project ps -q")
```

Run a zone service locally exactly like a realm one; it authenticates against the zone the current realm is bound to (or the `.beamable` `zid`).

```
beam_exec("project run --ids MyZoneService -q")
```

## Deploying to a Zone

`deploy plan` and `deploy release` default to `--scope realm`. Pass **`--scope zone`** to target the zone manifest (`cid.zid`); realm-scoped projects are then ignored, and only zone-scoped ones are included (and vice-versa). The chosen scope is persisted into the plan, so a later `deploy release --from-latest-plan` re-applies the same scope automatically.

```
beam_exec("deploy plan --scope zone -q")
beam_exec("deploy release --scope zone -q")
```
